# Copy to mirror.env and pass it with `docker compose --env-file mirror.env`.

# !!! UPLOAD CAPS: READ THIS FIRST !!!
# There is no upload cap by default. This mirror uploads as much as people ask
# for, over the web and over BitTorrent. If your hosting bills for traffic,
# that can cost a lot of money: set a monthly cap (and a daily one if you like)
# before you consent. Sizes are binary: 1T = 1024^4 bytes. `mirror status`
# shows what was uploaded today and this month. An existing mirror keeps the
# caps it already has; "none" removes a cap.
SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_EGRESS_MONTHLY=
SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_EGRESS_DAILY=

# Public DNS name pointing at this host; Caddy obtains its certificate.
SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_DOMAIN=mirror.example.org

# Optional contact published in this mirror's signed card.
SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_CONTACT=

# Nostr: the mirror posts its signed card (its address and a filter of the
# models it holds) to public Nostr relays, so Sovereign apps can find it. The
# relays see this server's address, which the card publishes anyway. "off"
# stops it. Comma-separated wss:// relays replace the default five.
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_NOSTR=off
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_NOSTR_RELAYS=wss://relay.example.org

# BitTorrent: the mirror shares its model files in Sovereign's own per-file
# swarms (listed on the BitTorrent DHT under this mirror's key, so anyone can
# look up which models it shares) and in matching Pirate Face torrents (each
# held model is looked up on pirateface.co). Peers see this server's address.
# Uploads count toward the caps above. "off" turns either part off.
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_BITTORRENT=off
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_PIRATE_FACE=off
# The port BitTorrent listens on, published by compose.yaml (TCP and UDP).
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_TORRENT_PORT=6881

# Disk budget for retained models (binary units: 1G = 1024^3 bytes).
# The default is 100G, as in compose.yaml and `mirror init`; raise it to carry more.
SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_BUDGET=100G

# Download budget per UTC day (default 50G); it protects this host's connection.
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_INGRESS_DAILY=50G

# A catalog that stops listing a model does not stop this mirror serving it:
# that is an advisory in `mirror status`, and you decide (block a copy to stop
# serving it). "on" is your opt-in to stop serving withdrawn copies
# automatically; it is reviewed policy. Unset keeps an existing mirror's choice.
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_FOLLOW_WITHDRAWALS=on

# Standing restart grant renewed at every start (at most 366d).
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_GRANT=180d

# Host directory with the reviewed collection.json and any source file it
# names, mounted read-only at /config.
SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_COLLECTION_DIR=./collection

# Optional: the starter collection, a signed one-time import list. Put
# the list file in the collection directory and give its published list ID
# (check it against docs/starter-collection.md). Imported models become this
# mirror's own selections: nothing published later can stop or change them.
# Small is about 10.6 GB, standard about 78 GB and large about 310 GB (each
# includes the smaller tiers): raise SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_BUDGET to fit. The Apple
# MLX builds are an opt-in add-on (gguf,mlx: about +6.9 GB small, +25.5 GB
# standard and up). With a starter list,
# collection.json is optional.
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_STARTER_LIST=/config/starter-list.json
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_STARTER_LIST_ID=LIST_SHA256
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_STARTER_TIER=small
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_STARTER_FORMATS=gguf
# If the review lists licences you must accept (non-commercial or makers' own
# terms), read them, then accept exactly those (comma-separated). Without it,
# a list with gated models is refused before anything is imported.
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_STARTER_ACCEPT_TERMS=gemma
# Optional: an extra source tried first for the starter bundles, such as a
# local copy mounted into the container (a store directory) or another mirror.
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_STARTER_MIRROR=/config/starter-store

# Leave empty to run plan-only: the review is printed and nothing is served.
# Set exactly to yes-i-consent-to-public-serving after reading the review
# (`docker compose logs mirror`). Serving is public and not anonymous.
SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_CONSENT=

# Optional: pin the exact image you verified (default: the 0.37.1 release tag).
#SOVEREIGN_MIRROR_IMAGE=ghcr.io/foxlight-foundation/sovereign-mirror@sha256:DIGEST
